ing \\(I=\\{2,3,\\dots ,n+1\\}\\) (i.e. removing **all** non\u2011sunny lines) gives  \n\n\\[\n\\mathcal L(I)=\\{S_c\\mid c=2,\\dots ,n+1\\},\n\\]\n\na set of \\(n\\) sunny lines.  \nBy the argument of \u00a72 the covering of \\(T_n\\) is still valid, so the case \\(k=n\\) is also realised.\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\n### 5. Conclusion  \n\nFor the given integer \\(n\\ge3\\) the admissible values of \\(k\\) are precisely  \n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\{0,1,2,\\dots ,n\\}} .\n\\]\n\nEvery such \\(k\\) is attained by the explicit families \\(\\mathcal L(I)\\) described above, and no other value of \\(k\\) is possible because the total number of lines is fixed to be \\(n\\)."

