t  \n\n   \\[\n   \\mathcal N_{n,k}= \\{\\,y=j\\mid 1\\le j\\le n-k\\,\\}\\;\\cup\\;\\{\\,x=n-k\\,\\}\n   \\]\n\n   consists of \\((n-k)+1\\) lines, i.e. **\\(n-k\\)** non‑sunny lines (the horizontal line \\(y=n-k\\) coincides with the vertical line \\(x=n-k\\) only at the point \\((n-k,n-k)\\) and is counted once).  \n\n   *Step 5 – final collection.*  \n   The required family of \\(n\\) distinct lines is  \n\n   \\[\n   \\mathcal L_{n,k}= \\bigl\\{L_1,\\dots ,L_k\\bigr\\}\\;\\cup\\;\\mathcal N_{n,k}.\n   \\]\n\n   It contains exactly \\(k\\) sunny lines (the \\(L_i\\)) and \\(n-k\\) non‑sunny lines (the members of \\(\\mathcal N_{n,k}\\)).  \n   By the arguments above every point of \\(T_n\\) lies on at least one line of \\(\\mathcal L_{n,k}\\).  \n   All lines are distinct because the sunny lines avoid the points of \\(S_k\\) and have slopes different from \\(0\\) and \\(-1\\), while the non‑sunny lines are axis‑parallel.\n\n5. **Conclusion.**  \n   The upper‑bound argument shows that no configuration can have more than \\(n-2\\) sunny lines.  \n   The explicit construction above shows that for every integer \\(k\\) with \\(0\\le k\\le n-2\\) a configuration with exactly \\(k\\) sunny lines exists.  \n\nHence the set of admissible values of \\(k\\) is precisely \\(\\{0,1,\\dots ,n-2\\}\\).\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\text{For all }n\\ge3,\\;k\\text{ is possible }\\iff 0\\le k\\le n-2.}\n\\]\n\n\n### Verification Task Reminder ###\n\nYour task is to act as an IMO grader. Now, generate the **summary** and the **step-by-step verification log** for the solution above. In your log, justify each correct step and explain in detail any errors or justification gaps you find, as specified in the instructions above.\n\n"
